0. DEFINITIONS

"Engine": Cramion as published by the Licensor: CramionCore, CramionFX,
CramionDM, CramionEditor, CramionUpdater, the player, tools, templates,
shaders, documentation and accompanying resources, in source and binary
form, including modified versions of them.

"Binaries": the executables, libraries, compiled shaders and files the
Licensor distributes in the Engine's downloadable package (for example,
Cramion-win64.zip).

"Source Code": the Engine's source code, in any form.

"Licensor": Josin (MantraxStudios), author and copyright holder of the
Engine.

"Product": a game, application, interactive experience, visualization
or content created WITH the Engine whose primary value is its own
content and not the Engine itself.

"Runtime": the parts of the Engine a Product needs in order to run (the
exported player, its libraries, and the shaders and data the editor
generates on export).

1. USE OF THE BINARIES (free of charge, royalty-free)

a) You may download and use the Binaries and the editor for any
   purpose, personal or commercial.
b) You may create Products and sell, publish or distribute them, for
   free or for a fee, on any store or platform, without paying
   royalties to the Licensor.
c) You may include the Runtime in your Products in compiled form.

2. SOURCE CODE (free of charge, copyright kept intact)

a) You may download, study, compile and use the Source Code for any
   purpose, personal or commercial.
b) You may modify it as you wish: fix, extend, trim or adapt the Engine
   to your needs, and use your modified version to create Products with
   the same rights as in section 1.
c) You may share the Source Code, original or modified, free of charge
   (for example, in a public repository), provided that:
   1. you keep intact the notice "Copyright (c) 2026 Josin
      (MantraxStudios)", this LICENSE file and the copyright notices in
      each file;
   2. you distribute it under this same license, without adding terms
      that contradict it;
   3. you clearly state that it is a modified version and not the
      Licensor's official version.
d) Your changes are yours, but the Engine they are based on remains the
   Licensor's work, and the Licensor keeps all copyright over it.

3. WHAT NOBODY MAY DO

a) Sell, rent, sublicense or charge in any way (including mandatory
   donations, subscriptions, "packs", paywalls or early access) for the
   Engine, the editor or their Source Code, original or modified,
   whether alone or inside a package, course, template or bundle whose
   main content is the Engine.
b) Redistribute the Binaries or the editor outside a Product (for
   example, re-uploading them to another website, store or server),
   except for the Runtime inside your Products.
c) Present the Engine, or a modified version of it, as your own work,
   or claim its original authorship.
d) Offer a modified version as if it were the official Engine.
e) Remove, hide or alter this license notice, the copyright notices or
   the Engine credits.
f) Use the name "Cramion", its logos or its visual identity for any
   product other than the official Engine, except as allowed in
   TRADEMARK.md.
g) Publish the Engine, or parts of its Source Code, on asset stores,
   marketplaces or other sales platforms.

4. ATTRIBUTION

Products do not have to show a Cramion logo or splash screen. It is
enough to include in their credits, or in a license file next to the
executable, the phrase "Made with Cramion Engine" and the third-party
notices the Runtime requires (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

5. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The Engine uses third-party libraries that keep their own licenses (see
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). This license does not restrict the rights
those licenses grant you over those components.

6. EARLIER VERSIONS

As of September 30, 2026, ALL versions of the Engine, including 1.4 and
earlier, are distributed solely under this license, wherever they are
downloaded from.

Anyone who obtained one of those versions under the MIT license before
that date keeps the MIT rights over that specific copy, provided the
copyright notice and the MIT license text are kept intact. Removing
those notices, or presenting the Engine as one's own work, leaves the
copy without any permission.

7. TERMINATION

If you breach this license, your rights end automatically. Products you
already released in compliance with it keep their permission to be
distributed. The Licensor may report any unauthorized copy or sale to
the relevant platforms and authorities.

8. NO WARRANTY

THE ENGINE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL
THE LICENSOR BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY ARISING
FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE ENGINE OR ITS USE.

9. CONTACT AND ADDITIONAL PERMISSIONS

For a commercial Engine license or any permission not covered here:
tupapienrakion1234@gmail.com.
